ontext Validation (IP Address)\", \"action\": \"Extract external IP addresses from the decoded 'scriptblock', 'get_recent_events', and 'get_recent_similar_alerts' results, then invoke 'check_ip_reputation' (AbuseIPDB) for each identified IP. This is only if they exist in the script or correlated data. If not, skip this step.\", \"tool_integration\": \"check_ip_reputation\", \"logic\": \"IP reputation is used as contextual enrichment only. Regardless of AbuseIPDB score, the presence of hard-coded external IP communication within scripts exhibiting reverse shell, command-and-control, or interactive execution behavior should be treated as malicious by behavior. Reputation data is used to strengthen confidence, identify infrastructure reuse, and support campaign correlation\\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201dnot to downgrade severity.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Final Triage Classification\", \"action\": \"Assign triage priority (LP or HP) by considering available context: process legitimacy, script behavior, execution environment, historical alerts, and network indicators if present.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - The user account executing the script is a known service or administrative account AND the script performs standard operational or maintenance tasks consistent with expected internal policies. \\n   - OR the script performs standard operational or maintenance tasks consistent with expected internal policies.\\n   - OR historical alerts show the same or similar scripts have executed previously without incident.\\n   \\n   > Note: LP does not require VirusTotal data, file paths, or IP reputation if they are unavailable. If those exist, they can optionally reinforce confidence.\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - The script shows unexpected or anomalous behavior outside normal administrative tasks.\\n   - OR the process is unknown, untrusted, or flagged as malicious (e.g., VirusTotal detections >=5).\\n   - OR command-and-control, reverse shell, or interactive execution behavior is observed.\\n   - OR the alert lacks context for critical operations and cannot be correlated with trusted service accounts or historical benign activity.\"}, {\"step_id\": 7, \"task\": \"Generate Investigation Summary\", \"action\": \"Construct a concise Description field including: 1) Script intent, 2) VT and AbuseIPDB results, if they exist, and 3) Final reasoning.\", \"logic\": \"Ensures the summary explicitly clarifies whether the triage was based on a physical file path or script behavior alone.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-9826\", \"alert_name\": \"Suspicious PowerShell Script Execution\", \"start_time\": \"2026-01-27T01:36:54.000Z\", \"source_ip\": \"10.5.14.92\", \"endpoint\": \"HR-SRV-02\", \"user\": \"k.tamm\", \"user_id\": \"S-1-5-21-88990011-22334455-66778899-1034\", \"description\": \"A suspicious PowerShell script was executed on the host.\", \"evidence\": {\"scriptblock\": \"Copy-Item 'C:\\\\Users\\\\*\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\Default\\\\Login Data' -Destination C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\chrome_cache.db -Force; Copy-Item 'C:\\\\Users\\\\*\\\\AppData\\\\Roaming\\\\Mozilla\\\\Firefox\\\\Profiles\\\\*.default-release\\\\logins.json' -Destination C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\ff_cache.json -Force\", \"os\": \"Windows Server 2019 Standard\"}}"
  }
]

