ontext Validation (IP Address)\", \"action\": \"Extract external (public) IP addresses from the decoded 'scriptblock', 'get_recent_events', and 'get_recent_similar_alerts' results, then invoke 'check_ip_reputation' (AbuseIPDB) for each identified IP. This is only if they exist in the script or correlated data. If not, skip this step, as sometimes there are only private IPs.\", \"tool_integration\": \"check_ip_reputation\", \"logic\": \"IP reputation is used as contextual enrichment only. Regardless of AbuseIPDB score, the presence of hard-coded external IP communication within scripts exhibiting reverse shell, command-and-control, or interactive execution behavior should be treated as malicious by behavior. Reputation data is used to strengthen confidence, identify infrastructure reuse, and support campaign correlation\\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201dnot to downgrade severity.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Final Triage Classification\", \"action\": \"Assign triage priority (LP or HP) by considering available context: process legitimacy, script behavior, execution environment, historical alerts, and network indicators if present.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - The user account executing the script is a known service or administrative account AND the script performs standard operational or maintenance tasks consistent with expected internal policies. \\n   - OR the script performs standard operational or maintenance tasks consistent with expected internal policies.\\n   - OR historical alerts show the same or similar scripts have executed previously without incident.\\n   \\n   > Note: LP does not require VirusTotal data, file paths, or IP reputation if they are unavailable. If those exist, they can optionally reinforce confidence.\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - The script shows unexpected or anomalous behavior outside normal administrative tasks.\\n   - OR the process is unknown, untrusted, or flagged as malicious (e.g., VirusTotal detections >=5).\\n   - OR command-and-control, reverse shell, or interactive execution behavior is observed.\\n   - OR the alert lacks context for critical operations and cannot be correlated with trusted service accounts or historical benign activity.\"}, {\"step_id\": 7, \"task\": \"Generate Investigation Summary\", \"action\": \"Construct a concise Description field including: 1) Script intent, 2) VT and AbuseIPDB results, if they exist, and 3) Final reasoning.\", \"logic\": \"Ensures the summary explicitly clarifies whether the triage was based on a physical file path or script behavior alone.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-9921\", \"alert_name\": \"Suspicious PowerShell Script Execution\", \"start_time\": \"2026-01-20T02:15:44.000Z\", \"source_ip\": \"192.168.1.45\", \"endpoint\": \"FS-PROD-02\", \"user\": \"NT SERVICE\\\\DataBackupAgent\", \"user_id\": \"S-1-5-80-3245\", \"description\": \"A suspicious PowerShell script was executed on the host.\", \"evidence\": {\"scriptblock\": \"param($TargetDrive = 'C:', $ThresholdGB = 10)\\n\\n# DataVault Backup - Pre-Scan Inventory Script\\n$LogPath = 'C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\DataVault\\\\Logs\\\\inventory_scan.log'\\n$ReportPath = 'C:\\\\ProgramData\\\\DataVault\\\\Temp\\\\large_files.csv'\\n\\nfunction Write-Log($Message) {\\n    $TS = Get-Date -Format 'yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss'\\n    \\\"[$TS] $Message\\\" | Out-File -FilePath $LogPath -Append\\n}\\n\\ntry {\\n    Write-Log 'Starting storage inventory scan...'\\n    $LargeFiles = Get-ChildItem -Path $TargetDrive -Recurse -File -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | \\n                  Where-Object { $_.Length -gt ($ThresholdGB * 1GB) } | \\n                  Select-Object Name, @{Name='SizeGB';Expression={$_.Length / 1GB}}, FullName\\n    \\n    $LargeFiles | Export-Csv -Path $ReportPath -NoTypeInformation\\n    Write-Log \\\"Scan complete. Found $($LargeFiles.Count) files exceeding threshold.\\\"\\n}\\ncatch {\\n    Write-Log \\\"Error during scan: $($_.Exception.Message)\\\"\\n}\", \"os\": \"Windows Server 2019 Standard\"}, \"technique\": {\"name\": \"File and Directory Discovery\", \"killchain_stage\": \"Discovery\"}}"
  }
]

