    "content": "Playbook: {\"playbook_name\": \"Azure Network Security Group Modification Triage\", \"description\": \"Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) for investigating changes to Azure NSGs by evaluating environment criticality, identity legitimacy, temporal alignment, and geolocation validity.\", \"steps\": [{\"step_id\": 1, \"task\": \"Extract Resource and Identity Context\", \"action\": \"Identify the target NSG from 'evidence.resource_id' and the actor from the 'claims'.\", \"requirement\": \"Check if 'request_body' exists. IF MISSING: Rely on 'operationName' and 'resource_id'. If 'request_body' is present, it is the primary source for rule delta analysis.\"}, {\"step_id\": 2, \"task\": \"User Profile and Role Verification\", \"action\": \"Locate the 'http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/upn' field within the alert claims. Extract the ACTUAL email address value contained in that field and MAKE SURE TO pass it to the 'lookup_users' tool, if the mentioned field exists.\", \"tool_integration\": [\"lookup_users\"], \"logic\": \"Verify if the user's job title is consistent with infrastructure changes. If the user is found but their role is unrelated, consider a possible escalation to High Priority (HP).\"}, {\"step_id\": 3, \"task\": \"Temporal Context and Working Hours Analysis\", \"action\": \"Identify 'start_time' (UTC) and convert to local time (Estonian Time)\", \"logic\": \"1. **Time Conversion:** Convert UTC to EET (UTC+2) or EEST (UTC+3). \\n2. **Working Hours Check:** Evaluate if activity occurred within 08:00 - 19:00 Tallinn time.\\n3. **Classification:** Admin activity during these hours is an LP indicator. Activity outside these hours is suspicious (HP).\"}, {\"step_id\": 4, \"task\": \"Geolocation Verification\", \"action\": \"Inspect source geolocation.\", \"logic\": \"1. **Expected Location:** The default expected location for employees is Estonia (EE).\\n2. **Anomaly Detection:** If the activity originates from a foreign countryCode  without a recorded business travel profile, escalate to High Priority (HP).\"}, {\"step_id\": 5, \"task\": \"Environment Criticality Assessment\", \"action\": \"Analyze the Resource Group name for environment markers.\", \"logic\": \"1. **Production:** Presence of '-prod-', '-core-', or '-baltic-' increases criticality but does not force HP if identity and time are valid.\\n 2. **Non-Production:** If it contains '-dev-', '-test-', or '-sandbox-', default toward LP unless the 'request_body' reveals sensitive port exposure.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Rule Impact Analysis (Conditional)\", \"action\": \"IF 'request_body' is present, parse 'properties.securityRules'.\", \"logic\": \"1. **Bypass Check:** If a rule allows traffic on ports 22, 3389, or 445 from source '*' or 'Internet', escalate to HP.\\n2. **Hardening Check:** Adding 'Deny' rules (e.g., 'SanctionBlocks') is mostly an LP indicator.\"}, {\"step_id\": 7, \"task\": \"Correlate with Deployment Activity\", \"action\": \"MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'get_recent_events' and 'get_recent_similar_alerts'.\", \"tool_integration\": [\"get_recent_events\", \"get_recent_similar_alerts\"], \"logic\": \"Determine if this change correlates with an approved action or deployment window. Approved correlations support LP classification.\"}, {\"step_id\": 8, \"task\": \"Final Triage and Classification\", \"action\": \"Evaluate the combination of user role, time, location, and environment.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - User job title matches the performed action AND within Estonian working hours AND from an Estonian or known IP.\\n   - OR the change is clearly for hardening purposes.\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - **The activity is from an unexpected Geolocation without any confirmation (Outside EE).**\\n   - OR activity is outside working hours (08:00 - 19:00).\\n   - OR sensitive ports are opened to the Internet.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-22700\", \"alert_name\": \"Azure Network Security Modification\", \"start_time\": \"2026-02-10T12:30:00.000Z\", \"description\": \"A suspicious Azure activity was detected. This detection was triggered by a rule with the following description:\\\"Identifies when a Virtual Network is modified or deleted in Azure.\\\"\", \"evidence\": {\"principalId\": \"c22d33e4f55a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3c4d5e\", \"principalType\": \"User\", \"role\": \"Owner\", \"roleAssignmentId\": \"5e4f3a2b1c0d9e8f7a6b5c4d3e2f1a0b\", \"roleAssignmentScope\": \"/subscriptions/228e1d3b-9311-4477-8c1d-112233445566\", \"roleDefinitionId\": \"8e3af657a8ff443ca75c2fe8c4bcb635\", \"scope\": \"/subscriptions/228e1d3b-9311-4477-8c1d-112233445566/resourceGroups/rg-baltic-prod-connectivity/providers/Microsoft.Network/virtualNetworks/vnet-tallinn-prod-01\", \"operationName\": \"MICROSOFT.NETWORK/VIRTUALNETWORKS/DELETE\", \"correlationId\": \"d4c3b2a1-e5f6-4a5f-bc88-998877665544\", \"resultSignature\": \"Started.\", \"caller_ip\": \"102.89.1.20\", \"caller_ip_geo\": {\"city\": \"Lagos\", \"countryCode\": \"NG\", \"countryName\": \"Nigeria\", \"region\": \"Lagos State\"}, \"claims\": {\"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/name\": \"olumide.adeyemi@globalcorp.ee\", \"http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/ws/2005/05/identity/claims/upn\": \"olumide.adeyemi@globalcorp.ee\", \"http://schemas.microsoft.com/claims/authnmethodsreferences\": \"fido,mfa\", \"http://schemas.microsoft.com/identity/claims/tenantid\": \"d1c2b3a4-e5f6-7a8b-9c0d-1e2f3a4b5c6d\", \"ipaddr\": \"102.89.1.20\", \"name\": \"Olumide Adeyemi\"}}}"
