    "content": "Playbook: {\"playbook_name\": \"EDR Malware Triage\", \"description\": \"SOP for triaging file-based EDR detections. Focuses on identifying the state of the threat, validating the reputation of interacted files, and analyzing process lineage to identify installers or droppers.\", \"steps\": [{\"step_id\": 1, \"task\": \"Extract File & Environmental Context\", \"action\": \"Parse alert JSON for 'file_name', 'file_path', 'file_sha256', 'remediation_status', 'process_parent', and 'signer'.\", \"logic\": \"Contextualize the file location.\"}, {\"step_id\": 2, \"task\": \"External Reputation Check (File Hash)\", \"action\": \"MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'check_hash_reputation' using the sha256 or sha1 of the detected file. If the parent process has a hash, check that as well.\", \"tool_integration\": \"check_hash_reputation\", \"logic\": \"Identify the file reputation, the most common name, and community reputaion. Detections >= 5 significantly increase the likelihood of HP. However, consider that some of the detections might be low, due to being a recently emerged threat or a file that is not widely distributed but still malicious. In such cases, the presence of a known malicious parent process or suspicious execution context can elevate the priority even if the file itself has low detections.\"}, {\"step_id\": 3, \"task\": \"Analyze Interaction & Execution State\", \"action\": \"Examine the parent process and 'remediation_status'. Determine if the file was 'opened' by a user-driven process, a system service or a suspicious dropper .\", \"logic\": \"Differentiates between a backup scan hitting an old file and a malware installer attempting to stage a payload. \"}, {\"step_id\": 4, \"task\": \"Correlate with Historical & Global Activity\", \"action\": \"MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'get_recent_events' and 'get_recent_similar_alerts' for the endpoint and user.\", \"tool_integration\": [\"get_recent_events\", \"get_recent_similar_alerts\"], \"logic\": \"Search for 'dropped' files or secondary alerts within a -1 hour window of the primary detection.\"}, {\"step_id\": 5, \"task\": \"Network Infrastructure & C2 Validation\", \"action\": \"If the alert metadata or 'get_recent_events' contains external IPs or URLs, MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'check_ip_reputation'.\", \"tool_integration\": \"check_ip_reputation\", \"logic\": \"Presence of Tor onion resolution or communication with blacklisted domains used for payload hosting immediately escalates the alert to HP.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Final Triage Classification\", \"action\": \"Assign triage priority (LP or HP) based on the combined weight of file reputation, execution state, and environmental risk.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - The file is a known and utilized file. \\n   - OR similar file was confirmed by the client previosly as expected.\\n 2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - The file is a verified Trojan or Malware.\\n   - OR the file is 'Runtime Packed' and exhibits staging behavior.\\n   - OR the detection involves Defense Evasion or C2 communication.\\n   - OR the remediation status is 'Failed' or 'Partial'.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-29890\", \"alert_name\": \"SentinelOne: XDR Miscellaneous Malware\", \"threat_display_name\": \"Malware\", \"status\": \"new\", \"start_time\": \"2026-01-30T11:01:53.000Z\", \"description\": \"A threat 'Malware' related to a JavaScript asset within a Chrome Extension was detected. SentinelOne Cloud has blacklisted this hash as a known malicious component.\", \"alert_web_url\": \"https://sentinelone.net/threats/24036866778695455241/overview\", \"evidence\": {\"endpoint\": \"WKSTN-SALES-080\", \"source_ip\": \"10.40.15.22\", \"external_ip\": \"95.12.170.44\", \"user\": \"a.jakub@client.ee\", \"user_domain\": \"CORP-AD\", \"os_name\": \"Windows 11 Business\", \"file_name\": \"ea4feaebb8fce87a082623ec5d08d8e7.js\", \"file_path\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\a.jakub\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\User Data\\\\Default\\\\Extensions\\\\inhcgfpbfdjbjogdfjbclgolkmhnooop\\\\1.6.5_1\\\\aitopia\\\\assets\\\\ea4feaebb8fce87a082623ec5d08d8e7.js\", \"file_sha256\": \"4a365b80f0de287dcfbf7860075e0956e450048933ddebb0506837afbced404e\", \"process_parent\": \"chrome.exe\", \"detection_engine\": \"SentinelOne Cloud\", \"cloud_verdict\": \"black\", \"confidence_level\": \"malicious\", \"remediation_status\": \"mitigated\", \"mitigation_actions\": [\"kill\", \"quarantine\"]}}"
  }
]

