        "text": "Playbook: {\"playbook_name\": \"Document Exposure & Threat Intel Triage\", \"description\": \"SOP for evaluating brand mentions within external datasets and leaked documents. NOTE: Field availability varies by source; 'matched_content', 'relative_paths', or 'document_title' may be missing. Triage must pivot based on available indicators. If any content or metadata is in a language other than Estonian, it must be translated before analysis.\", \"steps\": [{\"step_id\": 1, \"task\": \"Extract Available Metadata & Source Info\", \"action\": \"Parse alert JSON for all available evidence. This may include 'document_title', 'source_url', 'relative_paths', 'matched_content', and 'detection_source'.\", \"logic\": \"The logic must adapt to the specific data provided. In some cases, one field may be missing, requiring reliance on other indicators. For example, if 'matched_content' is absent, the analysis must focus more heavily on 'document_title', 'source_url', and 'relative_paths' for contextual clues.\"}, {\"step_id\": 2, \"task\": \"Language Detection & Translation\", \"action\": \"Check 'matched_content', 'document_title', and 'relative_paths' for non-English text. If the language is not English, translate it into English to ensure full contextual understanding.\", \"logic\": \"Accurate triage depends on understanding the specific intent and technical nature of the document. Misinterpretation due to language barriers can lead to false negatives or incorrectly prioritized alerts.\"}, {\"step_id\": 3, \"task\": \"Analyze Matched Content Sensitivity (If Available)\", \"action\": \"If 'matched_content' is present, scan for PII, PHI, Technical secrets, or Administrative labels.\", \"logic\": \"Content-based verification is the strongest indicator of intent. If missing, move to Step 4 and 5 for environmental and metadata analysis.\"}, {\"step_id\": 4, \"task\": \"Evaluate Source Platform Intent\", \"action\": \"Determine the reputation of the hosting platform. Is it a public repository, a developer paste site, or an anonymity-focused leak site?\", \"logic\": \"Platform context is a critical fallback when content is missing. A hit on a known breach-hosting Onion site is inherently higher risk than a hit on a public marketing repository.\"}, {\"step_id\": 5, \"task\": \"Perform Path & Vertical Context Check\", \"action\": \"Analyze 'relative_paths' and 'document_title' (if present). Determine if naming conventions align with the client's industry or a different vertical.\", \"logic\": \"Crucial for identifying 'Same Name, Different Industry' false positives. If the path suggests manufacturing or retail for a healthcare client, it is likely a false positive.\"}, {\"step_id\": 6, \"task\": \"Cross-Reference with Historic Alerting Patterns\", \"action\": \"MAKE SURE TO INVOKE 'get_recent_similar_alerts' to check if the available identifiers (URL, Title, or Path) have been flagged previously.\", \"tool_integration\": \"get_recent_similar_alerts\", \"logic\": \"Historical data is vital when current alert data is thin. Repeated false positives from a specific source suggest a persistent non-malicious context.\"}, {\"step_id\": 7, \"task\": \"Inspect Metadata for Internal Indicators\", \"action\": \"If a document is accessible, extract metadata to check for internal file paths or server naming conventions.\", \"logic\": \"Technical metadata exposure remains a primary pivot point for determining if a document is an accidental internal leak.\"}, {\"step_id\": 8, \"task\": \"Final Triage Classification\", \"action\": \"Assign triage priority (LP or HP) based on the combined weight of available evidence.\", \"logic\": \"Classification rules:\\n\\n1. **Low Priority (LP)** if:\\n   - **Vertical Divergence:** Titles/paths clearly indicate a different industry.\\n   - **Public Context:** Hosted on professional platforms with promotional titles, even if content is missing.\\n   - **Historical False Positive:** 'get_recent_similar_alerts' confirms a pattern of benign hits from the source.\\n\\n2. **High Priority (HP)** if:\\n   - **High-Risk Infrastructure:** Found on a known dark web breach repository or anonymous 'dump' site.\\n   - **Sensitive Metadata/Title:** 'document_title' or 'relative_paths' contain terms like 'DB_Dump', 'Credentials', or 'Confidential'.\\n   - **Structured Data:** 'matched_content' (if present) shows client-specific PII/PHI.\"}, {\"step_id\": 9, \"task\": \"Generate Investigation Summary\", \"action\": \"Construct a concise summary based on available fields. Explicitly note if translation was required and if the verdict was reached via metadata context due to missing 'matched_content'.\", \"logic\": \"Ensures the analyst understands the evidentiary limitations and the reasoning for the risk level assigned.\"}]}\nAlert: {\"alert_id\": \"SOC-75901\", \"alert_name\": \"Brand Mention in External Document\", \"threat\": \"DocumentExposure:VitalisHealthcare\", \"category\": \"Brand Monitoring\", \"status\": \"new\", \"start_time\": \"2026-02-19T18:12:05.000Z\", \"description\": \"Vitalis Healthcare mentioned in an external dataset or publication.\", \"evidence\": {\"detection_source\": \"TI-Monitor-Scribd\", \"document_title\": \"Vitalis_Internal_VPN_Config_v3.pdf\", \"source_url\": \"https://www.scribd.com/document/882145/vitalis-internal-infrastructure-guide\", \"matched_content\": \"...Access to the Vitalis Healthcare primary data center requires connection to the internal VPN gateway at 10.45.2.112. Authentication is handled via the Vitalis-DC01 domain controller. If the primary tunnel fails, technicians should failover to the secondary Cisco ASA node (v-asa-ext-02.vitalis.com) using the shared certificate stored in the /dev/certs/internal/ directory...\"}}"
